1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,070
You tap Send.

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,040
How does that message get from your phone

3
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:03,890
to your friend's?

4
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:06,794
First, it helps to know what the internet

5
00:00:06,794 --> 00:00:07,443
is.

6
00:00:07,804 --> 00:00:09,498
It isn't one big machine.

7
00:00:09,731 --> 00:00:12,540
It's lots of smaller networks connected together.

8
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:16,099
Your home Wi-Fi is one small network.

9
00:00:16,227 --> 00:00:19,059
Your internet provider connects it to other networks.

10
00:00:19,513 --> 00:00:21,672
Think of a street joining a main road,

11
00:00:21,672 --> 00:00:24,283
which joins roads leading across the city.

12
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,101
Your phone turns “Meet me at six” into

13
00:00:27,101 --> 00:00:28,400
digital data.

14
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:32,535
The internet carries data in packets—small bundles with

15
00:00:32,535 --> 00:00:33,741
an address attached.

16
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:36,307
A short text might fit in one packet;

17
00:00:36,436 --> 00:00:37,921
a photo needs many.

18
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:41,266
The address points toward the messaging service.

19
00:00:41,558 --> 00:00:44,239
At each network junction, a router checks that

20
00:00:44,239 --> 00:00:46,433
address and passes the packet along.

21
00:00:46,979 --> 00:00:49,300
No single router makes the whole trip.

22
00:00:49,476 --> 00:00:51,495
Each one handles the next step.

23
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,720
The messaging service knows which account belongs to

24
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:55,520
your friend.

25
00:00:55,881 --> 00:00:58,597
It sends the message through connected networks toward

26
00:00:58,597 --> 00:00:59,455
their phone.

27
00:00:59,746 --> 00:01:01,859
If they're offline, the app may wait for

28
00:01:01,859 --> 00:01:03,170
them to reconnect.

29
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:05,791
So the internet is really a team of

30
00:01:05,791 --> 00:01:07,822
networks passing data along.

31
00:01:08,113 --> 00:01:10,817
That's the journey behind one tap of Send.
